The attached image, Figure 5, demonstrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A, comprising flow cytometry dot plots, shows that when ovalbumin (OVA) is adsorbed to Nano-11, there is a marked increase in the uptake of both the nanoparticle and the antigen by BMDCs compared to soluble OVA or Nano-11 alone. Panel B, a histogram of FITC-OVA fluorescence, further illustrates that Nano-11-adsorbed OVA results in a greater shift in fluorescence intensity, indicating enhanced intracellular delivery of the antigen to the BMDCs, a crucial mechanism for vaccine adjuvants.